1
00:00:47,968 --> 00:00:49,344
(Sun Honglei)

2
00:00:49,728 --> 00:00:50,880
(Li Naiwen)

3
00:00:52,704 --> 00:00:54,272
(Guo Jingfei)

4
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:56,896
(Liu Yuning)

5
00:00:57,056 --> 00:00:59,325
(Gong Jun)

6
00:01:00,064 --> 00:01:00,864
(Chen Xingxu)

7
00:01:01,466 --> 00:01:04,064
(Wang Yuwen)

8
00:01:04,357 --> 00:01:06,432
(Lin Yi)

9
00:01:09,728 --> 00:01:12,352
=Wow The World S2=

10
00:01:12,493 --> 00:01:16,341
=EP08 Part 2=
(A wonderful holiday in Marseille)

11
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:32,080
Morning.

12
00:01:32,080 --> 00:01:32,400
Morning.

13
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:34,120
Morning, Honglei.

14
00:01:35,160 --> 00:01:36,360
What time did you go to bed last night?

15
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:37,360
Around 4 AM.

16
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:38,640
Weren't we seeing Lin Yi off?

17
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,080
At four o'clock, Lin Yi said
he couldn't stay any longer

18
00:01:41,080 --> 00:01:42,080
and really had to leave,

19
00:01:42,080 --> 00:01:43,600
(Lin Yi's reluctance)
then Lin Yi headed off.

20
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:47,960
Sailor Moon.

21
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:48,480
Hurry up.

22
00:01:49,344 --> 00:01:50,720
(I'm captivated by you)

23
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:51,600
I move away. Bye-bye.

24
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:51,960
Come on.

25
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:52,520
You take the center seat.

26
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:56,600
Alright. Everyone,

27
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:59,440
today is our second day in South France.

28
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:01,560
What do you think of this place?

29
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:02,480
So romantic.

30
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:03,280
So beautiful.

31
00:02:03,520 --> 00:02:04,560
Life in South France

32
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:06,600
moves at a laid-back pace
blessed by sunshine.

33
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:10,720
Slow down, immerse yourself
in local routine

34
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:12,640
and embrace life's true essence.

35
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:14,080
In Marseille,

36
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:17,000
this old town is bathed
in the Mediterranean breeze.

37
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:20,160
It blends the bold freedom of the ocean

38
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:21,880
with effortless French romance.

39
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:23,840
Every way you explore
holds its own charm.

40
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:25,760
No need to rush.

41
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:26,840
Slowing down

42
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:29,280
is the best way to understand this city.

43
00:02:29,760 --> 00:02:30,640
Today,

44
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:32,840
we will dive deep into a full day

45
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:34,040
of local life,

46
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:36,520
uncover Marseille's unique charms,

47
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:37,880
and cook

48
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:39,880
a cozy home-cooked dinner

49
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:41,080
full of warm worldly vibes together.

50
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:41,960
Okay.

51
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:42,520
Okay.

52
00:02:43,423 --> 00:02:44,855
I can't cook.

53
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:46,640
Can't cook is not an option.

54
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:48,200
But I am amazing at washing dishes.

55
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:49,240
(Kai has his own comfort zone)
No one does cleaner dishwashing than me.

56
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:51,120
(Nice to have support help)
That works then.

57
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:52,120
Next,

58
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:53,440
we'll carry out a mission.

59
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:54,240
Okay.

60
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:57,400
Within 100 seconds, eight of you need to

61
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:01,280
start with this line,
circle around the Earth Figure,

62
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:02,600
return to the starting line,

63
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:04,240
and deliver six balloons.

64
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:07,360
The whole team wins if all balloons
are delivered successfully.

65
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:09,320
But two of you

66
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:11,680
are Balloon Spirits,

67
00:03:12,320 --> 00:03:14,160
whose goal is to sabotage

68
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:15,400
the mission.

69
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:18,600
The two Balloon Spirits
don't know each other's identities.

70
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:21,280
If the Good People finish
three balloon deliveries

71
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:23,200
or correctly identify
both Balloon Spirits,

72
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:24,200
the Good People win.

73
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:27,160
Otherwise, the Balloon Spirits win.

74
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:28,200
Come draw your cards,

75
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:28,800
everyone.

76
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:30,280
We'll keep this fair, impartial
and transparent.

77
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:31,680
Okay, draw one card.

78
00:03:33,760 --> 00:03:34,320
Come on.

79
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:36,600
I'm a little nervous.

80
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:38,360
I just want to be a common villager.

81
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:39,254
(Wishing for a Good Person role)

82
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:42,480
Okay, finished.

83
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:45,840
Everyone, please close your eyes.

84
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:48,040
Number one, open your eyes.

85
00:03:48,531 --> 00:03:50,800
(Balloon Spirit: Liu Yuning)

86
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:51,720
Okay.

87
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:53,400
Number two, open your eyes.

88
00:03:53,746 --> 00:03:56,824
(Balloon Spirit: Yang Chaoyue)

89
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,280
Everyone, please open your eyes.

90
00:04:02,211 --> 00:04:03,622
(Looking for teammates)

91
00:04:05,332 --> 00:04:06,593
(Search in the same way)

92
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:07,600
Let's go.

93
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:08,120
Let's go.

94
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,080
Chaoyue, is it you?

95
00:04:12,960 --> 00:04:13,560
(Handle it calmly)
Not me.

96
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:14,280
Not you?

97
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:15,360
You look a bit suspicious.

98
00:04:15,570 --> 00:04:16,360
(The Balloon Spirit chosen by Jingfei)

99
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:17,360
You need some evidence.

100
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:21,360
Keep a close eye on Sun Honglei.

101
00:04:21,683 --> 00:04:22,720
(Suspected teammate?)

102
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:24,000
He's itching to stir up trouble.

103
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:27,720
Everyone face outwards.

104
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:29,840
But where to put it?

105
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:31,520
(Which position works best?)
Put it on our necks, like this.

106
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:31,760
(That's exactly what I want)
Okay.

107
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:33,640
Come on, you and me.

108
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:34,240
(A balloon delivered right to me)
The two of us?

109
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:36,080
I... No.

110
00:04:36,080 --> 00:04:37,400
(Due to height gap,
can't clamp the balloon)

111
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:38,000
The two of us... It's fine.

112
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:38,720
We can do it.

113
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:41,520
Jingfei, how about we two give it a go?

114
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:42,880
(Missed the balloon within reach)
Is this okay?

115
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:43,680
Okay.

116
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:47,480
Three, two, one, go!

117
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:47,760
Okay.

118
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:48,040
(Round 1)

119
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:48,640
Go.

120
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:49,960
Okay.

121
00:04:51,470 --> 00:04:53,286
(Guarding with the face)

122
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:56,600
(Matching face brake)

123
00:04:57,754 --> 00:04:58,940
(Ready to sabotage)

124
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:00,800
Don't pull us.

125
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:02,200
Let's go. We can walk faster.

126
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:03,120
(Balloon Spirit attempts to speed up)
Let's go.

127
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:04,320
There's not enough time.

128
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:06,320
Let's go.

129
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:08,480
We won't have enough time, friends.

130
00:05:09,425 --> 00:05:10,953
(Speeding up to sabotage the mission)

131
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:15,080
The balloon keeps sliding backward.

132
00:05:15,142 --> 00:05:16,681
(Gradually can't keep up)

133
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:17,280
(Weird-looking poses)

134
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:18,160
Don't run.

135
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:20,000
I can barely hold this pose steadily.

136
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:20,800
You know?

137
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:22,360
My pose is even harder.

138
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:24,320
(Totally lost control of facial expressions)
Someone is pushing me from behind.

139
00:05:25,189 --> 00:05:26,514
(Goal reached)

140
00:05:26,546 --> 00:05:27,871
(On the other side)

141
00:05:27,957 --> 00:05:29,389
(Ready to sabotage)

142
00:05:30,051 --> 00:05:31,131
(Giving up the position)

143
00:05:31,964 --> 00:05:32,990
(Grabbing in one go)

144
00:05:34,957 --> 00:05:35,791
(Shh, don't make a sound)

145
00:05:35,791 --> 00:05:36,881
(With Fei here, nothing can go wrong)

146
00:05:37,714 --> 00:05:38,826
(Forced it back into place)

147
00:05:39,232 --> 00:05:40,942
(Missed the opportunity)

148
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:43,160
Okay, Sun Honglei now wants to

149
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:45,280
make a move at the turn.

150
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:49,920
You, over there...

151
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:51,320
(Great misdirection)

152
00:05:51,597 --> 00:05:52,965
(Making another move)

153
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,040
Everyone, attention.

154
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:58,120
(Keeping a strict guard)
I can sense

155
00:05:58,120 --> 00:06:00,720
every little detail of Sun Honglei
right beside me.

156
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:02,040
(Immersively experiencing Sun Honglei)
What about your side?

157
00:06:02,883 --> 00:06:04,166
(Stepping backward hard to make room)

158
00:06:04,604 --> 00:06:05,716
(Very prominent)

159
00:06:05,801 --> 00:06:10,130
(I will carry you back to Beijing)

160
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:12,560
Someone is still pushing me from behind.

161
00:06:15,163 --> 00:06:16,243
(Sorry)

162
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:19,400
We're turning now.

163
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:21,480
(At the turning point)
I won't move. Yuning, you lead.

164
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:22,520
Me?

165
00:06:22,520 --> 00:06:23,360
I take the lead?

166
00:06:23,478 --> 00:06:24,200
(Are you sure?)

167
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:25,040
At the first turn,

168
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:26,320
Sun Honglei didn't make a move.

169
00:06:26,364 --> 00:06:27,400
(Let go)

170
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:27,760
Wait a moment.

171
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:29,360
I can't hold it in place anymore.

172
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:30,767
(Gradually can't hold on)

173
00:06:30,831 --> 00:06:31,601
(Still leaning back)

174
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:35,680
Why is it so crowded over here?

175
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:38,560
(My hands are giving out)
You can't use your hands for this game.

176
00:06:42,299 --> 00:06:42,940
(I did my best)

177
00:06:44,073 --> 00:06:44,640
(Finally let go)

178
00:06:44,640 --> 00:06:45,520
I saw him throw it.

179
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:46,400
Who dropped it?

180
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:47,760
No, he said I can't use my hands

181
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:48,360
to touch it.

182
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:49,560
Fei, it's you.

183
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:51,080
Fei is like this.

184
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,000
You didn't even try hard.

185
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:55,080
(What more am I supposed to do?)
Chaoyue is watching my every move.

186
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:56,040
When it was about to fall,

187
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:57,000
I even used my hand to steady it.

188
00:06:57,464 --> 00:06:59,680
(My teammate is Fei?)

189
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:00,480
It's really not me.

190
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:01,960
Chaoyue, you have to testify for me.

191
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:03,760
But what did you mean
by throwing it just now?

192
00:07:03,888 --> 00:07:04,775
(No matter the truth,
you're stuck taking the fall)

193
00:07:04,828 --> 00:07:06,324
(Only those who framed you know
how unjustly you've been wronged)

194
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:08,200
How exactly did it drop, Jingfei?

195
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:09,280
(Come clean)
I was right next to you.

196
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:11,000
(Become the target of public criticism)
I saw everything.

197
00:07:11,177 --> 00:07:11,640
(Lei's testimony)

198
00:07:11,640 --> 00:07:12,640
I can feel

199
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:14,040
the balloon we're holding together

200
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:15,520
(Lei's testimony)
is a little loose on his side.

201
00:07:15,623 --> 00:07:17,952
(Is the teammate
deliberately sabotaging?)

202
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:19,080
Well,

203
00:07:19,080 --> 00:07:20,440
you suspect me

204
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:21,280
just because it loosened a tiny bit?

205
00:07:21,280 --> 00:07:22,320
And you kept talking.

206
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:23,880
Why did you talk so much?

207
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:24,280
Why so many words all at once?

208
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:25,400
(Battle between Jingfei and Honglei)
Because I'm not.

209
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,400
I don't need to think.

210
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:28,600
What evidence do you have?

211
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:29,560
I was steady as an axle,

212
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:30,440
and didn't move at all.

213
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:31,920
(You say)
Can you vouch for me?

214
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:32,440
Yes.

215
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:33,960
He didn't move.

216
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:35,120
I didn't move at all.

217
00:07:35,120 --> 00:07:36,280
And I clamped it tight on both sides.

218
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:38,360
You didn't move because you didn't dare.

219
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:40,120
(Let me mention one thing)
First, the Balloon Spirits

220
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:41,960
don't know each other.

221
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:44,280
Is it possible they're out
to pin the blame on each other?

222
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:45,440
It's possible.

223
00:07:45,569 --> 00:07:46,937
(Nothing but Good People
doubting each other)

224
00:07:47,065 --> 00:07:48,825
(Just keep it going like this)

225
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:51,120
I'm just a common villager.

226
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:53,400
Both people beside me
are definitely Good People.

227
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:55,120
(Perfectly protecting the Balloon Spirit)
Maybe they just didn't stir up trouble this round.

228
00:07:55,188 --> 00:07:55,600
(Speak cautiously to conceal the role)

229
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:56,680
In this round, their performance...

230
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:57,440
Everything is fine for now.

231
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:58,280
Their actions are totally normal.

232
00:07:58,280 --> 00:07:59,480
Naiwen said, "Slow down."

233
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:00,800
"Let's walk more steadily."

234
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:02,120
I'm sure he is a Good Person,

235
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:02,880
in my opinion.

236
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:04,520
I think maybe in the first round,

237
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:05,960
the Balloon Spirits didn't make a move.

238
00:08:05,960 --> 00:08:07,200
But there were some accidents.

239
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:07,880
Yes.

240
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:08,840
(Really, it dropped accidentally)
It's indeed quite hard.

241
00:08:08,840 --> 00:08:10,520
Maybe the wind was a bit strong.

242
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,160
(Completely agree)
That's possible too.

243
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:13,600
Then who do you think it is?

244
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:14,760
I think it's Fei.

245
00:08:14,831 --> 00:08:15,708
(Wen's soft words with sharp intent)

246
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:18,000
Come on.

247
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:18,920
Please vote.

248
00:08:20,442 --> 00:08:21,949
(Round 1: Guo Jingfei is eliminated)

249
00:08:22,056 --> 00:08:23,146
(Protecting Fei for a bit)

250
00:08:23,317 --> 00:08:24,739
(No way to turn the tide)

251
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,240
Fei's role is...

252
00:08:29,847 --> 00:08:30,280
(Ready to claim victory)

253
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:30,760
Good Person.

254
00:08:33,748 --> 00:08:35,544
(Fei isn't my teammate)

255
00:08:35,811 --> 00:08:37,179
(Secretly delighted)

256
00:08:37,361 --> 00:08:38,600
(Successfully shifted the blame)

257
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:40,748
(Who exactly is my teammate?)

258
00:08:40,919 --> 00:08:42,720
The mission continues.

259
00:08:46,156 --> 00:08:47,717
(Giggling foolishly)

260
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:49,920
What are you laughing at?

261
00:08:50,837 --> 00:08:52,280
(Is it you, Lei?)

262
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:52,720
What are you laughing at?

263
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:55,400
Are you looking for your partner?

264
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:56,780
(Wise)

265
00:08:57,040 --> 00:08:58,000
What secret code are you two exchanging?

266
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,320
I notice he's looking for his partner.

267
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:01,040
Don't jump to baseless suspicion.

268
00:09:01,360 --> 00:09:02,560
Unlike this guy.

269
00:09:05,586 --> 00:09:06,591
(Round 2)

270
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:09,960
One, two.

271
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:11,840
You look like a big worm.

272
00:09:15,836 --> 00:09:16,915
(Leaning hard)

273
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:17,560
Don't.

274
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:19,080
Don't lean on me.

275
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:19,840
If you lean on me...

276
