845
00:25:24,200 --> 00:25:25,000
Ice cream experience.

846
00:25:25,840 --> 00:25:28,080
This is caramel. This is coffee.

847
00:25:30,240 --> 00:25:32,040
I think the pistachio one
should be good.

848
00:25:32,760 --> 00:25:33,320
Toffee.

849
00:25:33,600 --> 00:25:34,720
The toffee one is delicious.

850
00:25:35,920 --> 00:25:36,920
So happy.

851
00:25:37,034 --> 00:25:38,049
(Happiness starts from ordering)

852
00:25:39,760 --> 00:25:41,040
Chocolate is truly the best.

853
00:25:41,040 --> 00:25:41,240
Right?

854
00:25:41,240 --> 00:25:41,920
So delicious.

855
00:25:41,920 --> 00:25:42,360
Full of chocolate.

856
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:43,760
The milky one is delicious.

857
00:25:45,080 --> 00:25:45,920
I think this dark one,

858
00:25:46,440 --> 00:25:47,520
with a bit of bitterness, is delicious.

859
00:25:47,785 --> 00:25:48,320
(Eagerly)

860
00:25:48,320 --> 00:25:49,560
Who wants one more?

861
00:25:49,560 --> 00:25:50,040
I can.

862
00:25:50,136 --> 00:25:50,600
(Nai wants it, and Nai gets it)

863
00:25:50,600 --> 00:25:50,920
Here.

864
00:25:53,800 --> 00:25:54,600
So delicious.

865
00:25:55,320 --> 00:25:56,560
Let's take a selfie.

866
00:26:00,360 --> 00:26:00,920
Then let's go.

867
00:26:00,920 --> 00:26:02,080
Walk slowly, and eat slowly.

868
00:26:02,080 --> 00:26:02,360
Let's go.

869
00:26:04,920 --> 00:26:06,480
Really delicious. You ate it all?

870
00:26:08,520 --> 00:26:09,560
This should be enough for you, right?

871
00:26:10,154 --> 00:26:11,768
(Great satisfaction)

872
00:26:12,760 --> 00:26:14,520
There's a golden statue
on the top of the mountain on the left.

873
00:26:14,520 --> 00:26:15,520
I don't know if you saw it.

874
00:26:16,760 --> 00:26:18,280
You mean the one
on the distant mountain top?

875
00:26:18,280 --> 00:26:18,840
Yes.

876
00:26:19,132 --> 00:26:19,902
(Basilique Notre-Dame de la Garde
Located on the top of Garde Hill)

877
00:26:19,902 --> 00:26:20,280
(It offers a panoramic view
of Marseille and the Mediterranean)

878
00:26:20,280 --> 00:26:22,480
This is the landmark building
of the whole Marseille.

879
00:26:22,800 --> 00:26:23,920
The golden statue on the top

880
00:26:23,920 --> 00:26:26,440
of Basilique Notre-Dame de la Garde
is 9.7 meters tall.

881
00:26:26,440 --> 00:26:27,160
It's a Virgin Mary.

882
00:26:29,560 --> 00:26:30,920
The direction the Virgin Mary faces

883
00:26:30,920 --> 00:26:32,440
is the sea.

884
00:26:32,440 --> 00:26:34,560
The Virgin Mary
protects fishermen and sailors.

885
00:26:34,560 --> 00:26:35,520
So after they return,

886
00:26:35,520 --> 00:26:37,360
the first thing they do
is to show gratitude to the Virgin Mary

887
00:26:37,360 --> 00:26:38,520
by making their own boats

888
00:26:38,520 --> 00:26:39,600
into small models

889
00:26:39,600 --> 00:26:41,280
and hanging them inside the church.

890
00:26:43,640 --> 00:26:44,760
Sir, I have a question.

891
00:26:44,760 --> 00:26:46,760
Are these holes on the wall
bullet holes?

892
00:26:47,200 --> 00:26:48,040
These are bullet holes.

893
00:26:48,040 --> 00:26:49,040
If you walk around, you can also see

894
00:26:49,040 --> 00:26:50,240
the bullet holes from World War II

895
00:26:50,240 --> 00:26:50,760
all over there.

896
00:26:51,520 --> 00:26:51,840
Look.

897
00:26:52,960 --> 00:26:54,320
These spots.

898
00:26:55,840 --> 00:26:57,400
Were these made by aircraft gunfire?

899
00:26:57,400 --> 00:26:57,760
Yes.

900
00:26:58,440 --> 00:26:59,320
How come

901
00:26:59,320 --> 00:27:00,880
there's only this little mark?

902
00:27:00,880 --> 00:27:03,160
Because churches are always protected.

903
00:27:03,160 --> 00:27:04,480
This was hit by accident.

904
00:27:04,480 --> 00:27:06,640
In warfare,
churches are generally not targeted.

905
00:27:06,640 --> 00:27:07,880
Yes.

906
00:27:07,880 --> 00:27:09,320
It says the date right on there.

907
00:27:09,320 --> 00:27:11,400
it was bombed between August 15th

908
00:27:11,400 --> 00:27:12,840
and 25th, 1944.

909
00:27:18,480 --> 00:27:19,600
The one with the red roof

910
00:27:19,600 --> 00:27:20,760
is called Palais du Pharo.

911
00:27:21,320 --> 00:27:23,080
It was built by Napoleon III.

912
00:27:23,117 --> 00:27:24,277
(Palais du Pharo was a royal palace
ordered by Napoleon III in 1855)

913
00:27:24,277 --> 00:27:24,960
(It offers a panoramic view
of Marseille port and the Mediterranean)

914
00:27:24,960 --> 00:27:25,640
I see it.

915
00:27:28,920 --> 00:27:30,480
And that is Île d'If.

916
00:27:30,770 --> 00:27:31,480
(Château d'If, a limestone
island fortress located in Marseille)

917
00:27:31,480 --> 00:27:31,960
(Made famous by Alexandre Dumas' novel
The Count of Monte Cristo)

918
00:27:31,960 --> 00:27:33,040
The Count of Monte Cristo.

919
00:27:33,520 --> 00:27:34,800
He was imprisoned there.

920
00:27:47,480 --> 00:27:48,400
Should we

921
00:27:48,400 --> 00:27:49,840
take a selfie

922
00:27:49,840 --> 00:27:50,600
at the place with the best view?

923
00:27:50,600 --> 00:27:51,120
Come on.

924
00:27:51,520 --> 00:27:52,680
Come on, three, two, one.

925
00:27:54,640 --> 00:27:55,680
Let's go back and cook.

926
00:27:56,080 --> 00:27:56,560
Let's go.

927
00:27:57,000 --> 00:27:57,560
Hurry.

928
00:27:57,880 --> 00:27:58,440
Let's go buy groceries.

929
00:28:02,031 --> 00:28:05,387
(The two teams are shopping separately)

930
00:28:07,360 --> 00:28:08,280
I think onions...

931
00:28:08,280 --> 00:28:09,320
Two are enough, right?

932
00:28:09,352 --> 00:28:13,320
(Onion, green pepper, cucumber)

933
00:28:13,320 --> 00:28:13,720
I'll do it.

934
00:28:13,720 --> 00:28:15,120
(Scallions)
I need scallions.

935
00:28:15,743 --> 00:28:17,090
(Sniffing)

936
00:28:17,560 --> 00:28:18,400
Is this cilantro?

937
00:28:18,500 --> 00:28:19,720
(Kitchen novice asking)

938
00:28:19,720 --> 00:28:20,200
Cilantro?

939
00:28:20,819 --> 00:28:21,920
(Sniffing again)

940
00:28:21,920 --> 00:28:22,880
It looks like celery.

941
00:28:23,880 --> 00:28:24,840
It has no aroma whatsoever.

942
00:28:25,800 --> 00:28:27,160
If we can find peanut oil,

943
00:28:27,160 --> 00:28:28,320
we won't buy olive oil.

944
00:28:29,040 --> 00:28:30,680
Or we can just press oil
from peanuts ourselves.

945
00:28:30,962 --> 00:28:31,999
(Confused)

946
00:28:32,063 --> 00:28:33,837
(Smug)

947
00:28:34,440 --> 00:28:35,040
Press with what?

948
00:28:35,400 --> 00:28:36,480
With peanuts.

949
00:28:36,680 --> 00:28:37,360
Just press them hard.

950
00:28:37,360 --> 00:28:37,556
(Teasing Nai)

951
00:28:37,880 --> 00:28:38,360
(Can't believe it)
Peanuts...

952
00:28:40,645 --> 00:28:41,158
Peanut?

953
00:28:41,800 --> 00:28:43,200
Peanut oil is definitely pressed
from peanuts.

954
00:28:43,200 --> 00:28:43,960
It's very simple.

955
00:28:44,920 --> 00:28:46,280
We have the internet.

956
00:28:46,280 --> 00:28:47,080
What can't we find online?

957
00:28:47,080 --> 00:28:47,800
As long as there's a tutorial,

958
00:28:47,800 --> 00:28:48,920
there's nothing we can't make.

959
00:28:48,920 --> 00:28:49,521
I believe you.

960
00:28:49,521 --> 00:28:51,001
(Nai, you can do it)

961
00:28:53,726 --> 00:28:57,392
(Really searched)

962
00:28:57,960 --> 00:28:58,640
What's wrong?

963
00:28:58,640 --> 00:28:59,840
To get one pound of peanut oil,

964
00:28:59,840 --> 00:29:01,880
we need 2.5 pounds of peanuts.

965
00:29:02,240 --> 00:29:03,840
Stir-fry, crush, steam.

966
00:29:04,680 --> 00:29:05,760
Let's just buy it.

967
00:29:05,760 --> 00:29:06,760
(Why make things difficult
for ourselves)

968
00:29:06,760 --> 00:29:07,040
Yes.

969
00:29:07,040 --> 00:29:07,520
What do you think?

970
00:29:08,240 --> 00:29:09,160
Yes, I think so.

971
00:29:09,160 --> 00:29:09,480
Okay.

972
00:29:11,680 --> 00:29:13,400
Then I'll go buy the seafood.

973
00:29:13,400 --> 00:29:13,720
Okay.

974
00:29:14,240 --> 00:29:15,000
Tomatoes are okay,

975
00:29:15,037 --> 00:29:16,520
(Tomato)

976
00:29:16,520 --> 00:29:18,240
Make the stir-fried spicy cabbage?

977
00:29:18,240 --> 00:29:18,960
(Cabbage)
Okay.

978
00:29:19,056 --> 00:29:19,320
(Mushroom)

979
00:29:19,320 --> 00:29:20,320
Get some mushrooms.

980
00:29:20,880 --> 00:29:21,720
Do we need eggs?

981
00:29:22,880 --> 00:29:23,760
Get a tray of eggs.

982
00:29:24,320 --> 00:29:25,120
Since we bought tomatoes,

983
00:29:25,120 --> 00:29:26,360
not buying eggs would be weird.

984
00:29:26,360 --> 00:29:28,193
(Underlying code triggered)

985
00:29:28,240 --> 00:29:29,400
There are no mussels?

986
00:29:30,491 --> 00:29:32,597
(Searching around)

987
00:29:34,160 --> 00:29:35,320
How can there be no mussels?

988
00:29:35,320 --> 00:29:36,800
No mussels in Marseille?

989
00:29:37,256 --> 00:29:39,600
(Calling for help)

990
00:29:39,600 --> 00:29:40,120
Xingxu.

991
00:29:40,600 --> 00:29:41,040
Honglei.

992
00:29:41,600 --> 00:29:43,840
We don't have much meat here.

993
00:29:43,840 --> 00:29:45,920
You buy some meat there.

994
00:29:46,200 --> 00:29:47,600
Yes, ask them to busy some pork.

995
00:29:47,600 --> 00:29:48,320
Buy some pork.

996
00:29:48,560 --> 00:29:51,360
Then ask if they have mussels.

997
00:29:51,360 --> 00:29:52,080
Just these two things.

998
00:29:52,080 --> 00:29:52,600
One pound.

999
00:29:52,600 --> 00:29:52,960
Okay.

1000
00:29:52,960 --> 00:29:53,240
Bye-bye.

1001
00:29:53,240 --> 00:29:53,600
Okay.

1002
00:29:53,920 --> 00:29:54,280
Bye-bye.

1003
00:29:56,080 --> 00:29:57,120
Are these mussels?

1004
00:29:57,600 --> 00:29:58,800
Yes, these are mussels.

1005
00:29:58,800 --> 00:29:59,320
Green-lipped mussels.

1006
00:29:59,680 --> 00:30:02,320
I want 1.5 kilograms.

1007
00:30:04,640 --> 00:30:05,120
Yes.

1008
00:30:06,320 --> 00:30:07,360
Take it later.

1009
00:30:07,360 --> 00:30:07,840
Take it later.

1010
00:30:07,840 --> 00:30:08,640
I'll go buy some meat.

1011
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:08,960
Okay.

1012
00:30:09,720 --> 00:30:10,120
Thank you.

1013
00:30:11,200 --> 00:30:11,760
Bye.

1014
00:30:11,760 --> 00:30:14,128
(Pork)

1015
00:30:14,520 --> 00:30:15,240
Okay.

1016
00:30:16,160 --> 00:30:16,800
Where's the cilantro?

1017
00:30:17,200 --> 00:30:18,000
Cilantro?

1018
00:30:18,600 --> 00:30:19,240
Xingxu.

1019
00:30:19,600 --> 00:30:20,720
Naiwen wants cilantro.

1020
00:30:21,960 --> 00:30:22,440
(Got it)
Cilantro?

1021
00:30:22,880 --> 00:30:23,520
Get some cilantro.

1022
00:30:25,640 --> 00:30:26,080
Is it enough?

1023
00:30:26,080 --> 00:30:26,920
Yes.

1024
00:30:27,720 --> 00:30:29,200
Then put it in the cart first.

1025
00:30:29,200 --> 00:30:29,840
Let's go.

1026
00:30:30,480 --> 00:30:31,280
Okay, I think we're almost done.

1027
00:30:31,760 --> 00:30:32,000
Let's go.

1028
00:30:35,760 --> 00:30:36,720
Returning loaded with goods.

1029
00:30:41,240 --> 00:30:41,840
What are you doing?

1030
00:30:41,840 --> 00:30:42,960
Performing the peacock dance?

1031
00:30:42,960 --> 00:30:43,720
I am taking photos.

1032
00:30:43,720 --> 00:30:45,320
You can control the phone
with this watch.

1033
00:30:45,320 --> 00:30:45,920
You can also see the screen.

1034
00:30:45,920 --> 00:30:46,320
Look.

1035
00:30:46,680 --> 00:30:47,120
Do you want to join?

1036
00:30:47,440 --> 00:30:47,960
High-tech.

1037
00:30:47,960 --> 00:30:48,400
Come on.

1038
00:30:56,560 --> 00:30:58,360
Now, this cafeteria is...

1039
00:30:58,360 --> 00:30:59,480
(Cafeteria?)
Not this cafeteria.

1040
00:30:59,480 --> 00:31:01,400
This kitchen is my domain.

1041
00:31:01,816 --> 00:31:06,280
(Nai's Tiger Salad preparation begins)

1042
00:31:06,280 --> 00:31:06,760
Come on.

1043
00:31:07,840 --> 00:31:08,320
First,

1044
00:31:08,560 --> 00:31:10,440
we need to peel the cucumber.

1045
00:31:11,125 --> 00:31:13,604
(Nai's Tiger Salad, first step:
Peel the cucumber)

1046
00:31:14,120 --> 00:31:15,400
Nai, why are you doing it alone?

1047
00:31:16,840 --> 00:31:18,040
I'm peeling the cucumber.

1048
00:31:18,880 --> 00:31:20,160
What's wrong with these juniors?

1049
00:31:20,160 --> 00:31:21,120
They actually let Nai

1050
00:31:21,120 --> 00:31:22,360
peel the cucumber here.

1051
00:31:22,560 --> 00:31:22,920
Yes.

1052
00:31:22,920 --> 00:31:24,480
How can they let a white-headed old man

1053
00:31:24,480 --> 00:31:25,200
cook here?

1054
00:31:29,920 --> 00:31:31,640
With great power
comes great responsibility.

1055
00:31:31,640 --> 00:31:32,724
(No obligation to be modest)

1056
00:31:32,920 --> 00:31:34,040
Then do ours too.

1057
00:31:34,040 --> 00:31:34,400
Together.

1058
00:31:34,400 --> 00:31:34,720
(Easily holding on)
Okay.

1059
00:31:35,680 --> 00:31:36,040
Bye-bye.

1060
00:31:36,280 --> 00:31:37,040
Bye-bye, see you tomorrow.

1061
00:31:41,520 --> 00:31:42,400
I have to hold back a bit.

1062
00:31:42,400 --> 00:31:43,080
(Self-discipline gene awakening)
Can't eat.

1063
00:31:43,080 --> 00:31:45,040
Why am I so greedy this time out?

1064
00:31:45,840 --> 00:31:46,920
What do you mean "this time out"?

1065
00:31:46,920 --> 00:31:48,800
You were also quite greedy last time.

1066
00:31:48,800 --> 00:31:49,480
Was I greedy too?

1067
00:31:49,480 --> 00:31:50,160
Yes.

1068
00:31:50,160 --> 00:31:50,960
Yes, Honglei.

1069
00:31:50,960 --> 00:31:52,200
Did you notice last time?

1070
00:31:52,200 --> 00:31:54,080
It's already nowhere to hide.

1071
00:31:54,580 --> 00:32:00,127
(In that case, let's eat)

1072
00:32:00,683 --> 00:32:02,906
(Feeding)

1073
00:32:03,520 --> 00:32:04,520
Is it a fried dough twist?

1074
00:32:05,120 --> 00:32:05,600
Fried dough twist.

1075
00:32:08,240 --> 00:32:09,160
I want to eat meat.

1076
00:32:09,160 --> 00:32:09,920
But I think

1077
00:32:09,920 --> 00:32:10,600
I should hold back.

1078
00:32:13,320 --> 00:32:14,720
My

1079
00:32:14,720 --> 00:32:15,480
mussels

1080
00:32:15,480 --> 00:32:16,360
have to be cooked last.

1081
00:32:17,320 --> 00:32:18,280
Because my mussels

1082
00:32:18,280 --> 00:32:20,840
must be served hot to have wok hei.

1083
00:32:20,840 --> 00:32:21,920
So you guys make the main courses first.

1084
00:32:21,920 --> 00:32:23,440
I'll stew the curry first
and set it aside.

1085
00:32:23,440 --> 00:32:23,800
Okay.

1086
00:32:23,981 --> 00:32:24,600
(Yuwen's Curry Chicken in preparation)

1087
00:32:24,600 --> 00:32:26,000
Help me peel the potatoes
and put them there.

1088
00:32:26,720 --> 00:32:26,920
Okay.

1089
00:32:28,560 --> 00:32:28,920
I'm coming.

1090
00:32:28,920 --> 00:32:30,330
(Yuwen's Curry Chicken in preparation:
Potatoes in progress)

1091
00:32:31,280 --> 00:32:31,720
I'll do it.

1092
00:32:32,920 --> 00:32:33,640
You can shred it.

1093
00:32:34,040 --> 00:32:34,880
Okay, I'll shred it.

1094
00:32:34,880 --> 00:32:35,840
What are you going to make?

1095
00:32:35,840 --> 00:32:36,840
I can help you prepare the ingredients.

1096
00:32:37,440 --> 00:32:37,800
Okay.

1097
00:32:38,320 --> 00:32:40,080
Give me a piece of apple.
I'll stew it in the curry.

1098
00:32:40,800 --> 00:32:41,240
Okay.

1099
00:32:41,840 --> 00:32:42,400
(Yuwen's Curry Chicken in preparation:
Apple is ready)

1100
00:32:42,400 --> 00:32:42,640
Here.

1101
00:32:43,480 --> 00:32:43,680
Thank you.

1102
00:32:43,680 --> 00:32:44,160
Curry.

1103
00:32:44,448 --> 00:32:46,992
(Yuwen's Curry Chicken in preparation:
Cutting chicken into pieces)

1104
00:32:47,360 --> 00:32:48,040
Maybe I should chop it?

1105
00:32:48,360 --> 00:32:48,840
Then you can do it.

1106
00:32:48,840 --> 00:32:52,218
(Yuning comes to help)

1107
00:32:54,160 --> 00:32:54,640
Alright, done.

1108
00:32:55,800 --> 00:32:57,280
Our division of labor is quite funny.

1109
00:32:58,280 --> 00:33:00,480
Yuwen here is making curried potatoes,

1110
00:33:00,960 --> 00:33:02,000
and I'm helping her peel the potatoes.

1111
00:33:02,440 --> 00:33:03,000
Thanks, Nai.

1112
00:33:03,240 --> 00:33:04,400
I want to make Tiger Salad.

1113
00:33:04,760 --> 00:33:05,960
Deng Kai is helping me shred it.

1114
00:33:05,960 --> 00:33:07,920
And Yuning is helping Yuwen
cut the chicken.

1115
00:33:07,920 --> 00:33:08,520
Is it done, Nai?

1116
00:33:09,880 --> 00:33:10,560
Peel it outward.

1117
00:33:10,560 --> 00:33:11,720
Will it scratch your hand like this?

1118
00:33:12,640 --> 00:33:13,480
You mean like this?

1119
00:33:13,480 --> 00:33:13,880
Yes.

1120
00:33:16,480 --> 00:33:16,760
That makes sense.

1121
00:33:17,160 --> 00:33:18,320
I'm peeling the last one.

1122
00:33:18,320 --> 00:33:19,520
And you tell me to peel it outward.

1123
00:33:19,674 --> 00:33:21,908
(I just saw it too)

